    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter August 11th with a clear focal point in **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, who headlines our lineup with an elite 80.98 score. His matchup against Irvin presents an ideal confluence of high-upside variables: he commands the leadoff spot and benefits from a 14% boost due to a dynamic platoon advantage. Crucially, given our organization\u2019s mandate to prioritize speed, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**\u2019s combination of leadoff volume and the 87% stolen base probability against a slow-working delivery makes him our premier asset today. He is supported at the top of the order by **Junior Caminero** (75.54), who enjoys a favorable park factor and a solid xwOBA of 0.373, and **Yordan Alvarez** (73.01), whose elite 0.465 xwOBA maintains his floor despite a minor platoon drag against the lefty Whisenhunt.\n\nFrom a matchup perspective, we are aggressively exploiting the 5.37 xERA of the opposing starter facing **Nelson Velazquez** and **Yordan Alvarez**; the wind-out conditions at the park provide an added layer of confidence for their power profiles. Conversely, **Caleb Durbin** presents our most volatile spot. While he holds a respectable 43.26, he is drawing a tough assignment against Cease, whose 2.89 xERA severely limits our expectations. Our most difficult bench decision involved **Carson Benge** (52.26). While his score was sufficient for a start on a lighter day, he ultimately yielded to the higher positional efficiency of **Christian Yelich** (69.06) and **Lars Nootbaar** (65.16), both of whom benefit significantly from their respective platoon advantages and batting order positioning.\n\nRisk management remains a priority, as we continue to monitor the status of **Casey Schmitt**, who remains sidelined on the IL. While **Trea Turner** (66.35) remains an essential start, we are noting his 2% platoon penalty; however, his unique ability to leverage slow-delivery pitchers for stolen bases ensures he stays locked in the two-hole. With **Dillon Dingler** (47.75) serving as a marginal play due to his defensive focus and the specific platoon constraints against Bibee, we are effectively leaning on our top-order anchors to carry the load. We will continue to evaluate the depth chart, including prospects like **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Hector Rodriguez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez**, alongside veteran depth like **Josh Smith** and **Chase Meidroth**, to ensure our Roto floor remains protected. **Kazuma Okamoto** and **Gary Sanchez** remain unavailable, keeping our rotation locked to the current confirmed lineup.",
